        }
      }
    ]
  }
}', 'javascript' %>

#### Inspection errors

Status | Code | When
------ | ---- | ----
`400`  | `ParameterMissing` | `item` or `option` is missing
`404`  | `return_error` | The return does not exist or does not belong to your shop
`422`  | `item` | The return has no such item
`422`  | `inspection_state` | The item is not waiting for your inspection: it has none, it was already submitted, or Skroutz handles it
`422`  | `inspection_state` | A report of the item is being checked
`422`  | `option` | The item does not offer this option
`422`  | `service_report_file` | While the report is checked: no report was sent, the report sent was already found invalid, or the item takes no other report
`422`  | The param's name, e.g. `in_stock`, `service_report_file`, `additional_attachments` | The param is missing or invalid
`429`  |  | More than 30 requests with a report in 10 minutes

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "in_stock",
      "messages": [
        "must be answered for the selected service outcome"
      ]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

### Submit the physical review of a return

When the returned products are back at your shop, you report the condition each one came in: good, or
with a problem. A problem opens a compensation request for the item, or, where the return's
`customer_fault_outcome` is `return_to_customer` and the customer is at fault, sends the item back to
the customer as it is. This is the same action as the **product condition** form in the merchants'
panel, and it follows the same rules.

A return that can be reviewed carries a [`physical_review`](#physical-review), and so does each of the
line items the review covers. A return in state `pending_physical_review` holds the customer's refund
until the review is submitted or its `deadline` passes (`refund_on_hold`). A `returned` return can be
reviewed too, until its `deadline`. Once the review is submitted, or can no longer be, the return and
its items carry no `physical_review`.

A review is submitted once, for the whole return: send one `line_items` entry for **each** line item
that carries a `physical_review`, each exactly once. Send it as `multipart/form-data` when it carries
files; a review without files may be sent as JSON. The entries may be sent as an array
(`line_items[][id]`) or keyed by index (`line_items[0][id]`). The response is the updated return.

<pre class="terminal">
  POST /merchants/ecommerce/returns/:return_code/physical_review
</pre>

Param                                       | Type    | Description
------------------------------------------- | ------- | -----------
`line_items[_].id`                          | String  | The `id` of the line item. Required
`line_items[_].condition`                   | String  | `good` or `bad`. Required. A `good` item takes none of the params below
`line_items[_].quantity`                    | Integer | For a `bad` item: how many units have the problem, from 1 up to the item's `physical_review.max_quantity`
`line_items[_].reason`                      | String  | For a `bad` item: one of the item's `physical_review.reasons`
`line_items[_].at_fault`                    | String  | For a `bad` item: who is at fault, `customer` or `courier`
`line_items[_].comment`                     | String  | A description of the problem, up to 400 characters. Required when the reason's `comment_required` is `true`
`line_items[_].product_images[]`            | File    | Photos of the product: PNG or JPEG files, up to 5, each up to 7 MB. Required when the reason's `product_images_required` is `true`
`line_items[_].packaging_images[]`          | File    | Photos of the packaging: PNG or JPEG files, up to 5, each up to 7 MB. Required when the reason's `packaging_images_required` is `true`
`line_items[_].technical_assessment_report` | File    | A technician's assessment of the damage: one PNG, JPEG or PDF file, up to 7 MB. Required when the reason's `technical_assessment_report_required` is `true`, unless the customer is at fault and `customer_fault_outcome` is `return_to_customer`
`return_reason_correction[reason]`          | String  | Optional: the customer gave the wrong reason for the return. One of the return's `physical_review.return_reason_corrections`. The order is then left out of your shop's operational statistics
`return_reason_correction[comment]`         | String  | Required with `return_reason_correction[reason]`, up to 1000 characters

Files are checked by their name and by their content, so a file must really be the type its name says.

The request answers `200` with the updated return once the review is submitted. When the review changes
the return's state (`pending_physical_review` to `returned`), Skroutz also sends a
[return updated](/smart_cart/returns_webhook#return-updated) webhook.

While an item's `physical_review` carries a [`photo_check`](#photo-check), the photos of its problem are
checked before the review is submitted, and the request may answer `202` instead: see
[When the photos are checked](#when-the-photos-are-checked).

An order that came back without reaching the customer has no return. For its products,
[file a compensation request](/smart_cart/orders_api#file-a-compensation-request).

#### Example: one item in good condition, one with a damaged box

<pre class="terminal">
curl -X POST https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/returns/R-111111-1111111/physical_review \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here' \
  -F 'line_items[0][id]=lJxAnkMeQ8' \
  -F 'line_items[0][condition]=good' \
  -F 'line_items[1][id]=G87DAPeR3B' \
  -F 'line_items[1][condition]=bad' \
  -F 'line_items[1][quantity]=1' \
  -F 'line_items[1][reason]=damaged_packaging' \
  -F 'line_items[1][at_fault]=courier' \
  -F 'line_items[1][comment]=The box is crushed on one side.' \
  -F 'line_items[1][product_images][]=@product_1.jpg' \
  -F 'line_items[1][packaging_images][]=@packaging_1.jpg'
</pre>

#### Example: everything in good condition, with a corrected return reason

<pre class="terminal">
curl -X POST https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/returns/R-111111-1111111/physical_review \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here' \
  -d '{
    "line_items": [{ "id": "lJxAnkMeQ8", "condition": "good" }],
    "return_reason_correction": { "reason": "wrong_size", "comment": "The customer ordered the wrong size." }
  }'
</pre>

#### When the photos are checked

While an item's `physical_review` carries a [`photo_check`](#photo-check), Skroutz checks the photos of
its problem before it submits the review sent with them. The request stays the same, with two
differences:

* A `bad` item whose photos are checked must carry both `product_images` and `packaging_images`,
  whatever its reason requires.
* Photos that have to be checked are checked after the request answers. The request answers `202`
  with the return, the item's `photo_check.state` now `checking`, and the review is submitted once the
  check ends. You do not send it again.

What the request does depends on each checked item's `photo_check.state`:

The item's `photo_check.state` | Answer
------------------------------ | ------
`checking` | `422` `physical_review_state`, until the check ends
`valid` or `skipped` | `200`: the review is submitted with the photos already checked, whatever photos the request carries
`not_started`, `reused` or `unusable` | `202`: the photos sent are checked first

An item in good condition, and a problem with reason `return_not_received`, have no photos to check.

After a `202`, the outcome reaches you with a
[return updated](/smart_cart/returns_webhook#return-updated) webhook, or by retrieving the return:

The check | What happens
--------- | ------------
The photos pass | The review is submitted as you sent it. The webhook carries `changes.state` when the return's state changes, otherwise `changes.physical_review_submission`
The photos are refused | Nothing is submitted. The webhook's `changes.physical_review_photo_check` goes from `checking` to `reused` (the photos are the ones the customer sent with the return request) or `unusable` (the photos do not show the problem). Send the review again with other photos

Requests that send photos are limited to 30 per 10 minutes, and answer `429` past that.

##### Response when the photos are checked first

<pre class="terminal">
  Status: 202 Accepted
</pre>

<%= render_code '{
