#### Physical review errors

Every missing or invalid param of a request is answered at once, each under the param it is about, so
you can correct them all before sending the files again.

Status | Code | When
------ | ---- | ----
`400`  | `ParameterMissing` | `line_items` is missing
`404`  | `return_error` | The return does not exist or does not belong to your shop
`422`  | `line_items` | `line_items` is not exactly the line items that carry a `physical_review`, each once
`422`  | `physical_review_state` | The return takes no review now: it was already submitted, its `deadline` passed, or the products are not back yet. The message says which
`422`  | `physical_review_state` | The photos of an item are being checked
`422`  | `line_items.<id>.<param>`, e.g. `line_items.G87DAPeR3B.reason` | The param of the line item with this `id` is missing or invalid
`422`  | `return_reason_correction`, `return_reason_correction.reason`, `return_reason_correction.comment` | The order takes no correction, or its reason or comment is missing or invalid
`429`  |  | More than 30 requests with photos in 10 minutes

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "line_items.G87DAPeR3B.quantity",
      "messages": [
        "Check the quantity with a problem."
      ]
    },
    {
      "code": "line_items.G87DAPeR3B.product_images",
      "messages": [
        "The file format should be .jpeg, .jpg, or .png"
      ]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

### Watch a customer video

The `url` and `thumbnail_url` of a line item's [`user_videos`](#user-videos) point to the
following endpoints. Each takes your API token and redirects to the video's player page or its
thumbnail image, on a link signed for a short time. Request them when you need to show the video,
rather than storing the link they redirect to.

<pre class="terminal">
  GET /merchants/ecommerce/returns/:return_code/videos/:id
  GET /merchants/ecommerce/returns/:return_code/videos/:id/thumbnail
</pre>

Status | When
------ | ----
`302`  | Redirects to the player page or the thumbnail
`404`  | The video does not exist, is not yet uploaded, or does not belong to your return
`429`  | More than 60 video requests in a minute
`503`  | The video could not be signed. Try again later

## Error handling

In case of errors, the response will have a representative HTTP status code
in the `4xx` range. The body would contain an array of `errors`.

For example, if the requested return code does not exist (or does not belong to your shop),
you will get a `404` HTTP status code (Not Found):

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "not_found",
      "messages": [
        "Return not found"
      ]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

